WEBVTT

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:42.970
Everyone has a secret.

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:48.190
<i>Naturally, I am no exception.</i>

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:55.890
<i>I had as many choices as there are stars.</i>

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.320
<i>So what am I doing here?</i>

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:10.620
<i>By day, I fight alone as advisor 
to the Blood Donation Club.</i>

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.270
<b>Fight Alone</b>

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:12.270
<b>Strenuous Effort</b>

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.280
<i>It requires strenuous effort.</i>

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:17.760
<i>By night, I perform the backbreaking work 
of being the night school's only teacher.</i>

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.490
<b>Backbreaking</b>

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:21.630
<i>It leaves me covered in wounds.</i>

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:22.030
<b>Covered in Wounds</b>

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:26.840
<i>When I think back on it, 
my life has been unrewarding.</i>

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:31.660
<i>If I'd been more honest back then,</i>

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:36.460
<i>perhaps a different life 
would've awaited me.</i>

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:39.660
They didn't have any pork buns.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:44.580
What are you doing getting 
worked up by yourself?

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:47.130
Why did you show up all of a sudden?

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:48.660
All of a sudden?

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:51.610
You're the one who told me to 
bring you something to eat.

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:55.190
Oh, right. I'd completely forgotten.

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:58.600
I'm not your errand girl, you know.

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:02.450
It's rather inconvenient for 
you to casually contact me.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.940
Now, now. Don't be so uptight.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:11.630
I spend my weekends doing research. 
Put yourself in my shoes.

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:13.160
Don't you enjoy doing that?

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:15.170
Who would enjoy this?

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:18.580
I'm not like you, blood donation enthusiast.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:22.750
By the way, why were you 
talking to yourself?

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:25.400
What? Did I say something?

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:28.970
You said something about 
an unrewarding life.

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:32.470
It was the cry of my heart.

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:34.910
It's not something little 
kids would understand.

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:38.030
Huh. Well, I'm not particularly 
interested in understanding, anyway.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:47.000
Memories?

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:49.590
Don't touch that!

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:52.390
This is my soul!

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.220
Her soul?

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:00.670
Sounds kind of fishy.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:03.730
I bet it's something really expensive.

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:07.230
It might be something really rare.

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:10.770
Might be? You were satisfied 
with that and left?

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:14.870
She stuck it in the fridge and 
locked it right after that.

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:17.840
And after finishing the cup noodles, 
she had sweet buns and beer.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:22.000
Sweet buns and beer? Sounds nasty.

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:27.530
Stop drifting off-topic 
and answer my question.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:32.130
I already told you, she wouldn't 
tell me anything else about it.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:33.770
Sounds fishy.

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:35.810
Definitely fishy.

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:40.110
Maybe it's some kind of 
monster's blood again.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:42.690
Or her ex's.

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:46.650
What did you just say?

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.580
Or her ex's.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:50.390
What?!

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:53.570
Her ex's blood?

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:54.840
Definitely.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:57.550
And she has no sign of 
a boyfriend at her age.

00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:59.400
At her age? You know how old she is?

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:03.290
Judging by her skin, I think she's over 40.

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:04.640
And she's got a bad back.

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:06.650
And she's got those magnifying glasses.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:09.970
I bet she's staying faithful to that man.

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:11.930
What a wonderful story.

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:15.350
There's little point in us getting 
excited over speculation.

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:19.090
But I've never seen that 
color or thickness before.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:23.530
Regardless of whose blood it is, 
it's definitely a rare type.

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:27.680
In that case...

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:35.490
What do you mean, 
you're all out with stomachaches?

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:36.810
I'm sorry.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:40.340
We ate some pot stickers my 
neighbor gave us together.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:44.920
Nothing's more expensive than free, idiots.

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:47.170
They made me come here for no reason.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:56.180
That went well.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:58.770
I sent the boys a message 
telling them class is canceled

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:00.450
because the doctor has a stomachache.

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:04.760
Now we can investigate her secret 
without anyone bothering us.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:09.510
<i>More importantly, if it's high quality 
blood, then it's surely nutritious, too.</i>

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:11.910
<i>I bet it'd be good for Mai.</i>

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:14.000
I'm starting to get excited.

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:21.170
Then let's also film this documentary 
on Chihiro's true identity.

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:22.310
Let's ri—

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:27.230
I don't think so.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:30.300
What's wrong with you? 
Don't scare us like that.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.120
There's no class today.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:34.210
Didn't you check your messages?

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:37.800
I'm not that easily deceived.

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:46.960
<b>Sirloin</b>

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:39.880
Neither are we.

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:42.190
Sharing is caring.

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:44.200
Haven't you heard of the Antitrust Act?

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:46.160
Let us join you.

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:50.670
I can't believe you canceled classes. 
Just what are you planning?

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:56.140
As long as you're all here, 
could you handle the lights?

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:08.940
<b>School Infirmary</b>

00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:19.930
Chihiro installed a new lock.

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:22.570
Captain, you're up.

00:07:22.570 --> 00:07:23.750
Got it.

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:32.680
<b>CRACK</b>

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:31.680
<b>STING</b>

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:32.880
It didn't work.

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:36.100
Seriously? We're not getting anywhere.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.530
Perhaps we should ask him.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:44.100
<b>Franken-kun who will transfer
in Episode 10</b>

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:43.540
Franken, you're so wonderful.

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:48.270
Okay, that's enough.

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:50.980
Now then...

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:03.460
"I thought this might happen."

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:05.980
Haven't you guys heard of Shirou Sanada?

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:09.070
Doctor? I thought you left already.

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:12.590
You thought I'd be fooled by that lie?

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:15.570
How dare you underestimate me.

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:17.520
Don't be ridiculous.

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:21.900
You're after this blood, aren't you?

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:26.550
Even if nuclear war or a 
peasant uprising broke out,

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:30.400
I'd never let anyone take this blood.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:34.080
Please tell us about that blood 
that's so important to you.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:38.070
As youngsters on their way to 
becoming adults, offer us guidance.

00:08:38.070 --> 00:08:39.580
Please, doctor.

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:45.430
If you insist.

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:48.880
I hope you're prepared to listen all night.

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:54.240
It's a long story...

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:06.310
Our meeting was a shocking 
and moving affair.

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:12.020
I distilled old blood and made health 
supplements using the residue.

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:17.410
I sacrificed my youth for the 
sake of that experiment.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:18.440
Thanks again.

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:20.340
You're late.

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:23.290
How many hours does it take to 
deliver a cutlet bowl, you...

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:31.780
It's just falling in love.

00:09:32.650 --> 00:09:33.950
That was quick.

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:35.830
It certainly was shocking.

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:37.750
Shut up and listen!

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:48.510
He taught me what youth was.

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:53.380
Annual pass: 59,000 yen 
plus food and beverage costs.

00:09:53.770 --> 00:09:57.640
Arcade games: 35,600 yen 
plus food and beverage costs.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:03.310
Traditional Japanese games: 124,500 yen 
plus food and beverage costs.

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.000
Chimidoro Bank

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.000
Chihiro Chimatsuri-sama

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:13.460
He taught me that youth is expensive.

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:16.680
Then, one day...

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:18.160
Thanks again.

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:21.380
Jeez, you're late.

00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:27.130
He disappeared...

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:33.020
Goodbye

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:31.960
...along with my passbook and personal seal.

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:43.960
After a year and eight 
months of that, finally...

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:45.090
It's done!

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:52.050
It was the product of coincidence and a 
miracle, but my hard work finally paid off.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:56.780
The supplement I made without 
any trace of odd flavors, mold,

00:10:56.780 --> 00:10:59.650
or unwanted cultures provided enough 
energy to run a thousand meters.

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:02.300
Where can we buy that?

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.980
Shut up and listen until I'm finished!

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:17.560
At that time, I was seeing a 
man I'd met on a dating site.

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:23.410
If I apply for a patent, I'll be 
able to pay off all your debt.

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:26.310
Then we can get married.

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:30.230
Indeed. We'll build a new 
research lab together.

00:11:30.230 --> 00:11:33.850
He was a hematologist like me,

00:11:33.850 --> 00:11:38.420
but he carried a lot of 
debt from caring for his parents.

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:39.960
Debt?

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:41.950
Seriously?

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:44.910
This is starting to sound sketchy again.

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:49.170
I don't want to leave tonight.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:50.970
Chihiro...

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:55.870
Here's looking at you, kid.

00:11:56.850 --> 00:11:58.880
I've heard that line before.

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:03.620
It's from the 1942 American 
film <i>Casablanca</i>.

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:08.560
It's a line from the final scene of this immortal 
masterpiece and is exceedingly famous.

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:13.280
It stars Humphrey Bogart, and the 
heroine is played by Ingrid Bergman.

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:16.750
By the way, this beautiful actress was 
born in Sweden and is known for—

00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:28.180
Promise me you'll return.

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:29.520
Of course.

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:37.280
He left on a trip to pay off his debt.

00:12:38.350 --> 00:12:40.680
He made a promise to me.

00:12:41.810 --> 00:12:49.470
He promised he'd get fit and return with 
a gift of rare and valuable blood.

00:12:56.090 --> 00:12:59.880
Couldn't he have paid 
off his debt at an ATM?

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:02.300
Your story is full of anachronisms.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:05.910
Are you going to tell us he never returned?

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:07.210
He dumped you.

00:13:07.210 --> 00:13:08.510
It's marriage fraud.

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:10.550
Happens all the time.

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:14.310
The story is just beginning.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:29.970
I heard a rumor that he was living 
in a village in the north.

00:13:32.030 --> 00:13:37.300
He must've lost his memory 
in an accident or something.

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:25.620
Three winters ago, I found him covered 
in blood in front of my house.

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:30.410
Apparently he'd been beaten 
by some debt collectors.

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:35.610
He regained consciousness, but his 
rehabilitation took a long time.

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:40.430
Every night, he deliriously 
called a woman's name.

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:47.550
He hasn't forgotten me.

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:51.510
You must be Chizuru-san.

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:55.610
Chizuru?

00:14:55.610 --> 00:14:57.190
Who's Chizuru?

00:14:57.190 --> 00:14:59.360
Does that mean there was another woman?

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:02.380
Or he remembered your name wrong?

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:04.520
Either way, he's awful.

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:06.510
He totally dumped you.

00:15:06.510 --> 00:15:10.480
There's a movie that's not quite like this.

00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:13.090
And that movie is...

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:22.520
Master director Vittorio De Sica's 1970 
Italian/French/USSR joint production <i>Sunflower</i>.

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:26.260
It stars Sophia Loren and 
Marcello Mastroianni.

00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:30.410
In Japan, it's known as Sophia 
Loren's greatest masterpiece,

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:34.250
but personally, I prefer Lyudmila Savelyeva,

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:37.630
who played Mastroianni's Russian wife.

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:41.740
That aside, ultimately, it's marriage fraud.

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:44.140
Happens all the time.

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:47.820
Well, there's also something wrong 
with people who fall for it.

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:52.530
Back then, I was an idiot focused 
wholly on her research.

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:55.230
So, what happened to the supplement?

00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:59.740
What does this story have to do 
with the blood labeled "Memories"?

00:16:00.150 --> 00:16:01.890
Hold your horses.

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:04.700
This is where things get crazy.

00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:13.120
He'd lost his memory and was living 
a second life with a young woman.

00:16:13.930 --> 00:16:18.280
Not only that, but they had 
a cute child together.

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:37.640
Chiaki...

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:38.430
<b>Chiaki...</b>

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:42.050
Who's Chiaki? Isn't she Chizuru?

00:16:42.050 --> 00:16:44.380
There's another woman besides 
Chizuru, isn't there?

00:16:44.820 --> 00:16:48.320
Wait. There's a reason for this.

00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:53.850
Don't go, Chinami!

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:57.550
Yet another woman.

00:16:57.550 --> 00:16:58.560
Chinami.

00:16:58.560 --> 00:16:59.470
Chiharu.

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:00.460
Chifuyu.

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:03.140
Maybe there'll be a Chiiko, too.

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:06.160
Chiiko, we're leaving.

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:07.520
There really was one.

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:43.190
Months passed.

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:48.790
Once again I believed in miracles and 
devoted myself to producing supplements.

00:17:49.850 --> 00:17:51.420
Thanks again.

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:52.960
You're late.

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:57.090
How many hours does it take to 
deliver a cutlet bowl, you...

00:18:00.040 --> 00:18:04.230
It's just falling in love.

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:06.450
Again?

00:18:06.450 --> 00:18:08.690
Zero ability to learn.

00:18:13.350 --> 00:18:18.690
He taught me that youth is eternal.

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:23.270
Annual pass: 59,000 yen 
plus food and beverage costs.

00:18:23.270 --> 00:18:24.810
Okay, okay.

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:36.920
<b>School Infirmary</b>

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:26.910
We already heard that part.

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:30.790
Hurry up and tie this story 
to the "Memories" blood.

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:33.480
Before that, what happened 
to the supplement?

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:36.380
Did the debt collectors take it from you?

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:42.430
I'm glad you asked.

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:44.040
Of course we asked.

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:47.720
Several more months passed.

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:52.780
Once again I believed in miracles and 
devoted myself to producing supplements.

00:18:52.780 --> 00:18:53.730
Thanks again.

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:56.980
Shut up. I didn't order 
anything for delivery.

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:01.500
You let me in because I said 
was here to deliver something.

00:19:02.360 --> 00:19:03.590
I'm back.

00:19:03.980 --> 00:19:05.500
Again?

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:06.320
Chi...

00:19:06.900 --> 00:19:08.080
Tonio.

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:10.270
Tonio?

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:13.060
What? I just remembered his name.

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:13.500
<b>An Tonio</b>

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:18.130
I couldn't help what happened then.

00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:22.260
Those debt collectors didn't believe 
my story about the supplement.

00:19:22.580 --> 00:19:24.500
Where is it now?

00:19:24.840 --> 00:19:27.960
I'm sorry. They threw it in the gutter.

00:19:29.800 --> 00:19:32.090
They ganged up on me,

00:19:32.090 --> 00:19:36.300
and while living with Chiemi after 
she rescued me, this happened.

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:39.410
I made you wait all this time.

00:19:40.190 --> 00:19:42.240
But I still—

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:43.310
Don't say it.

00:19:44.750 --> 00:19:46.700
It's in the past now.

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:48.770
This was destined to happen.

00:19:50.320 --> 00:19:52.730
I couldn't keep our promise,

00:19:55.640 --> 00:19:57.530
but the winter is cold.

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:01.760
<b>*No animals were harmed in the making of this film.</b>

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:01.760
Inu

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:07.150
Let's start over again, Chi... Chi...

00:20:07.150 --> 00:20:08.860
What about Chiiko-chan?

00:20:08.860 --> 00:20:10.740
Isn't she your child?

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:13.590
I can't go back to how things were.

00:20:13.590 --> 00:20:15.240
Thanks again.

00:20:15.890 --> 00:20:19.970
Chi-chan, did you want kitsune 
soba for a late night snack?

00:20:20.430 --> 00:20:21.900
You were still seeing him?

00:20:39.620 --> 00:20:45.620
If only I'd told him not to go then...

00:20:59.220 --> 00:21:02.960
Well? Pretty good story, right?

00:21:02.960 --> 00:21:06.300
No. Listen, we'll give 
up on the supplement—

00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:09.790
That's right. Whose blood 
is the "Memories" blood?

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:10.770
Yeah.

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:20.970
Type A, type B, type O.

00:21:20.970 --> 00:21:22.990
None of them are rare or valuable,

00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:28.850
but it's the blood of those damn 
bastards who wasted my youth.

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:33.850
That plus all the rest of my youth 
is contained in this one bottle.

00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:42.730
Listen to the lamentation 
of my youth, damn it!

00:21:38.270 --> 00:21:42.740
<b>SLAP SLAP SLAP</b>

00:21:44.690 --> 00:21:46.940
Is her long-winded story finally over?

00:21:46.940 --> 00:21:49.160
Die, bastards!

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:48.910
<b>SLAP SLAP SLAP</b>

00:22:00.100 --> 00:22:03.370
Everyone has a secret.

00:22:05.500 --> 00:22:12.920
And not necessarily just one.

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:59.990
<b>Episode 9 "Bolt Style"</b>

00:23:46.900 --> 00:23:50.650
I just happened to come 
to this beach to swim.

00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:56.290
Excuse me for asking, but is 
there a doctor around here?
